🧠 5. Key Design Problem: Short Code Generation
This is the most important part.

✅ Approach 1: Auto Increment ID + Base62
Flow:

ID = 1000001
Convert to Base62 → abc123

Base62 chars:
[a–z, A–Z, 0–9] → 62 characters

Pros:
✔ Simple
✔ Predictable
Cons:
❌ Easy to guess (security risk)

✅ Approach 2: Hash (MD5/SHA)

Generate hash of URL
Take first 6–8 chars

Pros:
✔ Unique
✔ No sequence exposure
Cons:
❌ Collisions possible → must handle

✅ Approach 3: Random String

Generate random 6-character string

Pros:
✔ Highly secure
✔ Hard to predict
Cons:
❌ Need collision handling

✅ Best Practice:
Use Random/Base62 + collision check

